An element lies in the intersection of the recursively enumerable elements and the functional elements if and only if it belongs to the semigroup generated by R, L, and the bar combinator. This is Scott's semigroup theorem (Theorem 3.7): the countable semigroup of computable enumeration operators is finitely generated by those three elements.

One direction is the generation clause of Theorem 3.7. The other is that every semigroup-generated element lies in that intersection.
